# PART 9 - Keep It Working
## 9.1 Every day you work
§ When § Do this § Command or click
§ Start of session § Restore the VM if hibernated § Hyperstack > Virtual Machines > querymesh-gpu > Restore (Section 2A.13)
§ Start of session § Connect VS Code § VS Code > green button bottom-left > Connect to Host > querymesh-gpu
§ Start of session § Check the three services § `docker ps` (vllm, opensearch) and `curl -s localhost:4566/_fakecloud/health`
§ Start of session § Start FakeCloud if it is not running § `nohup fakecloud --storage-mode persistent --data-path ~/fakecloud-data > ~/fakecloud.log 2>&1 &`
§ Start of session § Re-attach your tmux session § `tmux attach -t qm`
§ End of session § Save your code to GitHub § `git add -A && git commit -m "WHAT YOU DID" && git push`
§ End of session § Hibernate the VM (stops GPU billing) § Hyperstack > querymesh-gpu > Hibernate
§ End of a real-AWS session § Tear everything down § Section 6B.15

## 9.2 Back up
- Code: GitHub (Section 2B.13). Push at the end of every session.
- Secrets: keep a copy of .env in your password manager. Never commit it (it is in .gitignore).
- OpenSearch data: it lives in the Docker volume opensearch-data. You can always rebuild it by running the ingestion again, so no backup is needed for learning.
- Airflow settings: ~/airflow (re-created by airflow standalone if lost).

## 9.3 Update safely
- Python packages are pinned in pyproject.toml. To update one: change its version, run `uv pip install -e ".[dev,ingest]"`, run `pytest -q`, then try `python -m querymesh.graph "test question"`.
- Docker images: change the tag in scripts/start_vllm.sh or scripts/start_opensearch.sh, run the script again.
- Kubernetes: build a new image tag (v2), run `helm upgrade` with `--set image.tag=v2`; roll back with `helm rollback querymesh 1`.

## 9.4 Undo
§ What went wrong § Undo
§ You broke a Python file § `git checkout -- querymesh/FILE.py` (back to the last commit)
§ A bad Helm upgrade § `helm history querymesh -n querymesh` then `helm rollback querymesh REVISION -n querymesh`
§ Bad data in the index § `curl -X DELETE localhost:9200/arxiv-chunks` then `python -m querymesh.search setup` and ingest again
§ A wrong answer is stuck in the cache § wait 24 hours, or delete it: `python -c "from querymesh import cache; cache._client.delete(cache.cache_key('THE QUESTION'))"`
§ FakeCloud state is a mess § `pkill fakecloud && rm -rf ~/fakecloud-data && mkdir ~/fakecloud-data`, start it again
§ kind cluster is a mess § `kind delete cluster --name querymesh` then Section 6B.4 again

# PART 10 - Troubleshooting
§ Symptom § Likely cause § Exact fix (steps)
§ `ssh: connect to host ... port 22: Connection timed out` § VM not ACTIVE, wrong IP, or SSH rule missing § 1. Hyperstack > querymesh-gpu: status must be ACTIVE. 2. Copy the IP again (it can change after Restore). 3. Firewall tab: add TCP 22 if missing. 4. Update the HostName line in your SSH config.
§ `httpx.ConnectError` to localhost:8000 or 401 from vLLM § vLLM is still loading, crashed, or LLM_API_KEY differs § 1. `docker logs --tail 50 vllm` and wait for "Application startup complete". 2. Check that .env LLM_API_KEY is the same value the script used (re-run scripts/start_vllm.sh after changing it).
§ `ConnectionError` to localhost:9200 § OpenSearch not running or vm.max_map_count too low § 1. `docker ps -a` shows opensearch? 2. `docker logs --tail 30 opensearch`. 3. If it says max virtual memory areas too low: `sudo sysctl -w vm.max_map_count=262144` and run scripts/start_opensearch.sh again.
§ Jina returns 401 or 402 § key missing, wrong, or free tokens used up § 1. `grep JINA .env`. 2. Open https://jina.ai/embeddings/ and check the key balance. 3. If the error mentions the task name: set `EMBED_MODEL=jina-embeddings-v3` in .env and recreate the index (Part 9.4 "Bad data").
§ Search returns 0 hits § nothing ingested yet, or index created with another dimension § 1. `curl -s localhost:9200/arxiv-chunks/_count`. 2. If count is 0: run Section 4.5. 3. If you changed EMBED_DIM: delete and recreate the index.
§ `illegal_argument_exception ... search pipeline` § the RRF pipeline does not exist § run `python -m querymesh.search setup`
§ arXiv `HTTP 429` or empty results § too many requests or a too narrow query § wait 1 minute; never run two ingestions at the same time; test the query on https://arxiv.org/search/advanced first
§ The graph stops with `GraphRecursionError` § the supervisor kept looping § check MAX_RETRIEVALS and MAX_GENERATIONS in .env are small numbers (2); read the steps printed to see which agent repeats
§ Remote mode: `AgentCardResolutionError` § one agent is not running, so discovery cannot read its Agent Card § `curl -s localhost:8102/.well-known/agent-card.json` for each port 8101-8105; start the missing one (Section 6A.3)
§ API returns 401 § token missing, expired (60 min) or JWT_SECRET changed § get a new token with POST /token; all API replicas must share the same JWT_SECRET
§ Cache never hits § REDIS_URL empty or not starting with rediss:// § `python -c "from querymesh import cache; print(cache._client)"` must not print None; copy the URL from the Upstash Details page again
§ `kind load docker-image` says image not present § you built with a different name or tag § `docker images | grep querymesh` and use exactly that name:tag
§ Pod stuck in `CreateContainerConfigError` § the Secret querymesh-secrets does not exist § kind: Section 6B.9 FakeCloud column; EKS: `kubectl get externalsecret -n querymesh` must show SecretSynced
§ Ingress has no ADDRESS on EKS § AWS Load Balancer Controller not running or no permissions § `kubectl -n kube-system get pods | grep aws-load-balancer` and `kubectl -n kube-system logs deploy/aws-load-balancer-controller | tail`
§ GitHub Actions: `Not authorized to perform sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity` § the trust policy sub does not match the repo § check the repo name in deploy/aws/github-oidc-trust.json; new repos may use the immutable sub format (SPEC note in 6B.14)

# PART 11 - Practice Projects
## 11.1 Easy - Add a sixth agent: the Summariser
Goal: an agent that turns the final answer into 3 bullet points for Telegram.
Requirements: a new skill function, a new entry in AGENTS (port 8106) with its own Agent Card, a new node in the graph that runs after the critic says grounded, a test with a fake skill.
Success criteria: pytest passes; the Agent Card at port 8106 lists the skill; Telegram replies show the bullets; the supervisor still finishes in under 12 steps.
## 11.2 Medium - Semantic cache next to the exact cache
Goal: also reuse answers for questions that mean the same thing ("What is RRF?" and "Explain reciprocal rank fusion").
Requirements: store question vectors in a second OpenSearch index; on a cache miss, search it with k=1 and reuse the answer if similarity is above a threshold you choose; log hits in Logfire; keep the SHA-256 cache as the first, fastest check.
Success criteria: on 20 paraphrased questions, at least 50% hit the semantic cache, and a manual check of 10 hits finds no wrong reuse.
## 11.3 Hard - Production hardening on EKS
Goal: QueryMesh survives load and failures on EKS.
Requirements: HorizontalPodAutoscaler for the API and writer; PodDisruptionBudgets; HTTPS on the ALB with an ACM certificate; per-user rate limiting in the API; OpenSearch with persistent EBS storage; a GitHub Actions job that runs the Part 7 evaluation and fails the deploy if the grounded rate drops by more than 5 points.
Success criteria: a 10-minute load test at 5 requests/second with p95 latency under 30 s and no 5xx; deleting any one pod causes no failed request; the pipeline blocks a deliberately worse prompt.

# PART 12 - Cheat Sheet
## Part 2 - connect and set up
```
ssh -i $env:USERPROFILE\.ssh\querymesh-key ubuntu@VM_IP
tmux new -s qm          (new session)    tmux attach -t qm    (come back)
Ctrl+b c  new window    Ctrl+b n  next window    Ctrl+b d  detach
curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh
cd ~/querymesh && uv venv -p 3.12 .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
uv pip install -e ".[dev,ingest]"
python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
bash scripts/start_vllm.sh        docker logs -f vllm
bash scripts/start_opensearch.sh  curl -s localhost:9200
nohup fakecloud --storage-mode persistent --data-path ~/fakecloud-data > ~/fakecloud.log 2>&1 &
source scripts/use_fakecloud.sh   |   source scripts/use_aws.sh
aws sts get-caller-identity
```
## Part 4 - ingestion and search
```
python -m querymesh.embeddings
python -m querymesh.search setup
python -m querymesh.ingest --query "cat:cs.CL AND abs:retrieval" --max-papers 5
python -m querymesh.ingest --query "all:agents" --max-papers 5 --abstracts-only
python -m querymesh.search "How does reciprocal rank fusion work?"
curl -s localhost:9200/arxiv-chunks/_count
aws s3 ls s3://querymesh-papers/pdfs/
source ~/airflow-venv/bin/activate && export AIRFLOW_HOME=~/airflow && airflow standalone
cat ~/airflow/simple_auth_manager_passwords.json.generated
```
## Part 5 - agents, graph, cache
```
python -m querymesh.llm
python -m querymesh.graph "What are recent methods to reduce hallucination in RAG?"
pytest -q
python -c "from querymesh import cache; print(cache.cache_key('What is RAG?'))"
```
## Part 6A - servers, tracing, API, UIs
```
python -m querymesh.agents retriever     (also grader, writer, critic, scout)
curl -s localhost:8101/.well-known/agent-card.json | jq
uvicorn querymesh.api:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8090
TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST localhost:8090/token -d "username=admin&password=API_PASSWORD" | jq -r .access_token)
curl -s -X POST localhost:8090/ask -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"question":"What is RRF?"}' | jq
curl -N -X POST localhost:8090/ask/stream -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"question":"What is RRF?"}'
python -m querymesh.ui_gradio     python -m querymesh.ui_telegram
```
## Part 6B - containers, Kubernetes, AWS
```
docker build --target app -t querymesh:v1 .
docker build --target ingest -t querymesh-ingest:v1 .
docker compose up -d     docker compose ps     docker compose logs -f api     docker compose down
kind create cluster --config deploy/k8s/kind-config.yaml
kind load docker-image querymesh:v1 querymesh-ingest:v1 --name querymesh
helm lint deploy/helm/querymesh
helm upgrade --install querymesh deploy/helm/querymesh -n querymesh --create-namespace -f deploy/helm/querymesh/values-kind.yaml
kubectl -n querymesh get pods
kubectl -n querymesh port-forward svc/querymesh-api 8090:80
kubectl -n querymesh create job first-ingest --from=cronjob/querymesh-ingest
eksctl create cluster -f deploy/aws/eksctl-cluster.yaml
kubectl -n querymesh get ingress
eksctl delete cluster -f deploy/aws/eksctl-cluster.yaml
```
## Part 7 - evaluation
```
python -m querymesh.evaluate build --n 30
python -m querymesh.evaluate retrieval
python -m querymesh.evaluate e2e --n 10
```
## Key facts
§ Fact § Value
§ Ports § vLLM 8000, Airflow 8080, API 8090, OpenSearch 9200, FakeCloud 4566, agents 8101-8105, Gradio 7860
§ RRF score § sum over result lists of 1 / (60 + rank)
§ Agent Card URL § http://AGENT/.well-known/agent-card.json
§ MCP SSE URL § http://AGENT/mcp/sse
§ A2A URL § http://AGENT/a2a
§ Cache key § querymesh:answer: + SHA-256 of (LLM_MODEL + "|" + lower-cased, space-normalised question)
§ Cache lifetime § 86,400 seconds (24 hours)
§ JWT lifetime § 60 minutes, HS256, secret JWT_SECRET
§ Loop limits § MIN_RELEVANT 2, MAX_RETRIEVALS 2, MAX_GENERATIONS 2
§ FakeCloud account § 123456789012, keys test/test, endpoint http://localhost:4566
§ Hyperstack billing § SHUTOFF bills, HIBERNATE does not bill the GPU, DELETE stops everything

# PART 13 - Self-Test
1. What happens if you ask a question about a topic that is not in your index at all? List the agents that run, in order.
2. Do this: compute the RRF score (rank constant 60) of a chunk that is rank 2 in BM25 and rank 5 in vector search.
3. What happens if you change EMBED_DIM from 1024 to 512 in .env but keep the old index?
4. What happens if two people ask "What is RAG?" and "what  is   rag?" one minute apart?
5. Do this: write the curl command that fetches the Agent Card of the critic agent.
6. What happens if the scout agent is down while the retriever finds only 1 chunk (remote mode)?
7. Why does the API keep working when Upstash Redis is unreachable?
8. Do this: write the command that runs the ingestion CronJob once, right now, on the kind cluster.
9. What happens if you hibernate the Hyperstack VM and later restore it: which services come back by themselves and which do you start by hand?
10. Why does the GitHub Actions workflow need `id-token: write` and no AWS keys?

